e Go unit tests for the prompt package, and handle edge cases that might require temporary filesystem manipulation\n- For the empty loops and missing loops scenarios, I'll use filesystem operations with cleanup to test those conditions\n- The test structure should follow the spec requirements: use `build_and_get_rick_bin.py` for the binary and run `go test ./internal/prompt/...` for unit tests\n\nWriting test script... Writing build execution logic... Checking that SPEC and OKR template literals are properly removed from the dry-run output, then moving on to run the Go unit tests for the prompt package. Writing test logic... Writing test logic... I need to check what `build_and_get_rick_bin.py` actually returns to make sure I'm handling the output format correctly, so let me look at that file to see if it provides a JSON with the bin_path.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec569ff7-ba83-4b88-9084-35285316906b","uuid":"95fb29fa-6311-4625-b995-c60c9e495a57"}
